  "details": "For networked map features that are sensitive to both delay and latency--like playing music notes--relying on Udon synced variables forces me to architect stuff in pretty weird ways. I'd love to be able to do event-driven networked map features.\n\nSendCustomNetworkEvent() is really close, but can't send any data, just a blank procedure call.\n\nFor my use case (sending MIDI notes with timestamps), I need to send about 32 bits of data, ASAP.\n\nAn additional hardcoded method for something like `SendCustomNetworkEvent(NetworkEventTarget target, string eventName, UInt32 data)` would be amazing, and hopefully not too much extra overhead. An extra argument with the network timestamps would be super cool too.\n\nIf yall do decide to do this, a version that takes 4 separate byte args as data would be potentially even more useful.\n\nThey'd be like tiny tiny network packet \"registers\" and let me skip packing stuff into ints.",
